              "_Go then, my little Book, and show to all\par
              That entertain and bid thee welcome shall,\par
              What thou dost keep close shut up in thy breast;\par
              And wish what thou dost show them may be blest\par
              To them for good, may make them choose to be\par
              Pilgrims better, by far, than thee or me.\par
              Tell them of Mercy; she is one\par
              Who early hath her pilgrimage begun.\par
              Yea, let young damsels learn of her to prize\par
              The world which is to come, and so be wise;\par
              For little tripping maids may follow God\par
              Along the ways which saintly feet have trod._"\par
\par
                                     Adapted from JOHN BUNYAN.\par
