                        THE HISTORY OF A SQUASH.\par
\par
    Once upon a time a farmer planted a little seed in his garden,\par
    and after a while it sprouted and became a vine, and bore many\par
    squashes. One day in October, when they were ripe, he picked one\par
    and took it to market. A grocer-man bought and put it in his\par
    shop. That same morning, a little girl, in a brown hat and blue\par
    dress, with a round face and snub nose, went and bought it for\par
    her mother. She lugged it home, cut it up, and boiled it in the\par
    big pot; mashed some of it, with salt and butter, for dinner;\par
    and to the rest she added a pint of milk, two eggs, four spoons\par
    of sugar, nutmeg, and some crackers; put it in a deep dish, and\par
    baked it till it was brown and nice; and next day it was eaten\par
    by a family named March.\par
