                              A SAD ACCIDENT.\par
\par
    On Friday last, we were startled by a violent shock in our\par
    basement, followed by cries of distress. On rushing, in a body,\par
    to the cellar, we discovered our beloved President prostrate\par
    upon the floor, having tripped and fallen while getting wood for\par
    domestic purposes. A perfect scene of ruin met our eyes; for in\par
    his fall Mr. Pickwick had plunged his head and shoulders into a\par
    tub of water, upset a keg of soft soap upon his manly form, and\par
    torn his garments badly. On being removed from this perilous\par
    situation, it was discovered that he had suffered no injury but\par
    several bruises; and, we are happy to add, is now doing well.\par
                                                                 ED.\par
