                                A LAMENT\par
\par
                           FOR S. B. PAT PAW.\par
\par
        We mourn the loss of our little pet,\par
          And sigh o'er her hapless fate,\par
        For never more by the fire she'll sit,\par
          Nor play by the old green gate.\par
\par
        The little grave where her infant sleeps,\par
          Is 'neath the chestnut tree;\par
        But o'er _her_ grave we may not weep,\par
          We know not where it may be.\par
\par
        Her empty bed, her idle ball,\par
          Will never see her more;\par
        No gentle tap, no loving purr\par
          Is heard at the parlor-door.\par
\par
        Another cat comes after her mice,\par
          A cat with a dirty face;\par
        But she does not hunt as our darling did,\par
          Nor play with her airy grace.\par
\par
        Her stealthy paws tread the very hall\par
          Where Snowball used to play,\par
        But she only spits at the dogs our pet\par
          So gallantly drove away.\par
\par
        She is useful and mild, and does her best,\par
          But she is not fair to see;\par
        And we cannot give her your place, dear,\par
          Nor worship her as we worship thee.\par
