\par
LITTLE BUTTON ROSE. Illustrated. 12mo. 50 cents.\par
\par
     A bright, vivacious child visits her maiden aunts. Her\par
     influence on the somewhat narrow characters about her is\par
     delightfully described.\par
\par
POPPIES AND WHEAT. Illustrated. 12mo. 50 cents.\par
\par
    Two girls travel through Europe. The frivolous Ethel learns the\par
    advantages of culture and simple dignity from her companion.\par
\par
MOUNTAIN-LAUREL AND MAIDENHAIR. Illustrated. 12mo. 50 cents.\par
\par
    The story of a New Hampshire farmer's daughter who is fond of\par
    writing verses.\par
\par
PANSIES AND WATER-LILIES. Illustrated. 12mo. 50 cents.\par
\par
    "Pansies" is a story of a girls' discussion of books;\par
    "Water-Lilies" is a romance by the sea-shore.\par
\par
THE DOLLS' JOURNEY. Illustrated. 12mo. 50 cents.\par
\par
    A droll account of the travels of two dolls. ("Shadow-Children"\par
    and "The Moss People" in same volume.)\par
\par
MORNING GLORIES AND QUEEN ASTOR. Illustrated. 12mo. 50 cents.\par
\par
    Aunt Wee changes Daisy from a petulant to a cheerful girl by\par
    interesting her in the wonderful world of nature which Daisy has\par
    never before learned to appreciate justly.\par
\par
THE LITTLE MEN PLAY.\par
THE LITTLE WOMEN PLAY.\par
\par
    Adapted from Miss Alcott's famous stories, "Little Men" and\par
    "Little Women," by Elizabeth L. Gould. Illustrated. 12mo. Price\par
    50 cents each.\par
\par
    Two forty-five minute plays of two acts each, for eight or ten\par
    little people. They will prove a source of limitless delight.\par
